### Visual Studio Code
#
# The shared editor configuration is committed (c_cpp_properties.json,
# extensions.json, settings.json), so ignoring the whole directory only
# dropped *new* files silently: anything added there later would never be
# tracked. Ignore the per-user files instead.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json

### JetBrains IDEs (CLion, IntelliJ, etc.)
.idea/
.idea_modules/
out/

# CMake generated build directories
cmake-build-*/

### Visual Studio
.vs/
*.vcxproj.user
*.vcxproj.filters
*.rsuser
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb

# Visual Studio build results
#
# These were copied from a Visual Studio template and were unanchored, so
# `[Dd]ebug*/` matched any directory whose name starts with "debug" at any
# depth. It silently ignored real source: `.agents/skills/debug-inference/`
# never reached the repository, and a future `src/debug/` would not either.
# Anchor them to the repository root to keep the intended meaning (build
# output next to the project file) without swallowing source trees.
/bin/
/obj/
/Debug/
/Release/
/x64/
/x86/

